ae={are thermodynamically stable and durable below 500 K. They can be stored for any length of time at room temperature, if their analytical use is planned. and  and The efficiency of AEs emission correlate with a variety of physicochemical parameters, among them with the volume is of the hydration layer of the of leaving group during CL process. and  and Original analytical tests were developed with the use of new indicators and markers based on AE. and  and Acknowledgments and  and The studies were financed by the Polish State National Science Center through the grants No. N N204 375740 (contract No. 3757/B/H03/2011/40) for the period 2011-2014 and No. UMO-2012/05/B/ST5/01680 for the period 2013-2015. and  and References and  and 1. Kricka LJ. Anal. Chim. Acta 2003;500:279-286. and  and 2. Zadykowicz B, Krzymiski K, Storoniak P, Baejowski J. J. Therm. Anal. Calorim. 2010;101:429-437. and  and 3. Nizioek A, Zadykowicz B, Trzybiski D, Sikorski A, Krzymiski K, Baejowski J. J. Mol. Struct. 2009;920:231-237. and  and 4. Krzymiski K, Og A, Malecha P, Roshal AD, Wrblewska A, Zadykowicz B, Baejowski J. J. Org. Chem. 2011;76:1072-1085. and  and 5. Krzymiski K, Roshal AD, Zadykowicz B, Biak-Bieliska A, Sieradzan A, J. Phys. Chem. A 2010;114:10550-10562. and  and 6. Kozin YI, Dyubko TS, Sokolyk OA, Roshal AD, Krzymiski K. ArchivEuromedica, 1st & 2nd Edition, 2011;91-93. and },
