abstract={The rates of ingestion, egestion, ammonium excretion, and CO sub(2) respiration of Tripneustes gratilla (Echinodermata: Echinoidea) from a shallow water embayment at eastern Mactan Island, central Philippines were examined. There was no significant difference in weight-specific feeding rate with the three macrophytes (Sargassum polycystum, Thalassia hemprichii, and Kappaphycus alvarezii). The power function equation, M=KWb fitted well with the weight-specific egestion rates (r super(2) = 0.93), weight-specific CO sub(2) respiration rates (r super(2) = 0.92) and ammonium excretion rates (r super(2) = 0.86). Weight-specific egestion rates, CO sub(2) respiration and ammonium excretion were indirectly proportional to body weight. For weight-specific egestion rate (in mu g DW faeces/g DW urchin-h), the regression coefficient, b and constant, K were -2.31 plus or minus 0.68 (mean plus or minus SE) (P = 0.02) and 6359.55 ~c5394.31 (P = 0.29), respectively. The b and K for CO sub(2) respiration were -1.28 plus or minus 0.48 (P - 0.04) and 39.72 plus or minus 10.59 (P = 0.01), respectively. For ammonium excretion, the b and K were -1.03 plus or minus 0.46 (P = 0.11) and 262.51 plus or minus 56.89 (P = 0.02), respectively.},
