abstract={Experiments were conducted at 28-30 degree C to study the growth rate and introgen excretion of young red snapper Lutjanus argentimaculatus. In group 1, a dry pellet diet was used as food; in group 2, flesh of shrimp Penaeus monodon; and in group 3, flesh of round scad Decapterus maruadsi. The specific growth rate (SGR) of group 1 was 4.19% per day, and those of group 2 and group 3 were 3.83% and 3.90% per day respectively. The rations of nitrogen excretion were also different among the three groups, Group 1 was 4.080; group 2, 3.759; and group 3, 3.869 mg-N per fish per day. The relationships between nitrogen excretion (NE) and nitrogen intake (NI) of three groups were all linear, viz. NE sub(1) = 2.107 + 0.310NI sub(1), NE sub(2) = 1.749 + 0.316NI sub(2), NE sub(3) = 10879 + 0.348NI sub(3).},
