month={NA},
abstract={Nitrogen recycling in oceanic environments is considered on a cost to benefit basis; recycling efficiency (R) defines the ratio of total heterotrophic nitrogen regeneration to the rate of phytoplankton grazed. A simple model is derived which demonstrates that R is a function of the excretion to ingestion ratios of organisms at each trophic level as well as the length of the food chain. R is discussed in relation to ecological efficiency, and model equations are solved for relative production, regeneration and egestion for 1-5 trophic levels using and ecological efficiency characteristic of an oceanic environment. Analysis of the microbial loop on the basis of recycling efficiency indicates that marine microheterotrophs may not contribute is much to nitrogen regeneration as previously suggested. The ecological role of nitrogen recycling os discussed in relation to the maintenance of nutrient-sufficient relatively high growing algal population in oceanic waters depleted of inorganic nitrogen.},
