abstract={Bio-assays have been made with diatoms dominant in oyster-ponds to estimate the algal growth potential of the waters of the Baie de Bourgneuf (Vendee). Data obtained showed that the presence of oysters in the culture waters resulted in a greater algal production. It has also been observed that oyster-waters are enriched by dissolved organic nitrogen. Indirect estimations showed that diatoms are able to take up important concentrations of organic nitrogen. The authors have incubated oysters, Crassostrea gigas . Oysters are seen to excrete nitrogen in ammoniacal and organic forms such as urea, amino acids and other substances. The nitrogen source can be used directly by three dominant oyster-pond diatoms, consequently increasing biomass production.},
