month={NA},
abstract={The fine structure, biochemical, and physiological characteristics of two species of Chlorella isolated as endosymbionts from larger Foraminifera have been examined. The strain isolated from Amphistegina lessonii (A1 - 2) did not grow in either the nitrate or thiamine-supplemented ammonium test media and was not further characterized physiologically. In fine structure it was distinct from Chlorella nana, C. spaercki, C. marina , and C. stigmatophora , four marine species recently studied in the TEM. It was closer in fine structure to C. ovalis and C. salina but could be clearly distinguished from both by the fine structure of its cell wall. On the basis of the information at hand isolate A1-2 is not clearly identifiable with a known species of Chlorella . The physiological and fine structural attributes of the organism isolated from Heterostegina depressa suggest that it is a halotolerant strain of C. saccharophila Krueger.},
