year={1981},
volume={14},
month={NA},
abstract={super(14)C-U-glucose utilization is measured by the rate of decrease of its concentration in the medium, k, and the rate of tracer uptake by themicroorganisms, k'. Both rates are postively correlated with total biomass evaluated by C sub(p), P sub(p), chl and ATP. The ratio k/C sub(p) is negatively correlated with the C/P ratio of dissolved organic matter (DOM). The percentage of respired glucose, R%, correlates negatively with the C/N/P ratio of DOM. k and R% are influenced by light. Dissolved organic carbon (DOC) excretion by phytoplankton is determined by the super(14)C method. Excretion is correlated with particulate production, relative excretion is negatively correlated with biomass and irradiance. In situ DOC concentrations do not vary through out the day. Their correlation with N and P inorganic forms hints at the existence of a refractory part of the total DOM. The authors try to establish the DOC budget and to evaluate heterotrophic production.},
