abstract={Addition of nutrients to aquatic media leads to rapid development of phytoplankton and other primary producers, while the presence of particulate organic matter is followed by the appearance of bacteria, including vibrios, such as V. anguillarum and V. parahaemolyticus. In 5 areas studied, vibrios were distributed on the particulate matter rather than in the water phase. To determine the role of primary producers as source of nutrients for vibrios, bioassays were carried out with green and red algae as nutrient source and a culture of V. anguillarum as substrate consumer, the 2 components being separated by a dialysis tube such that the photosynthetic excretion products could diffuse freely from algae to vibrios. The excretion products had a stabilising effect on the population size of the vibrios and the excreted carbon could maintain the vibrios for a long time.},
