year={1976},
volume={76},
month={NA},
abstract={The strong correlation of the paucity of nutrients in warm seas and the occurrence of symbiosis between various benthonic animals and zooxanthellae there is interpreted as a nutrition economical recycling process. As zooxanthellae increase the calcification ratio in lime- secreting animals, especially in corals, the symbiosis yields the sideeffect that the algae-enhanced skeleton growth enables these hermatypic corals to compensate for destructions by waves and bioerosion and to build the framework of coral reefs.},
