month={NA},
abstract={6 algal spp (green algae, diatoms, dinoflagellates) were studied. P sub(min) assimilation in the dark by cells non-low in phosphorus is shown for the majority of the spp (except for Phaeodactylum tricornutum, Goniaulax polyedra). Phosphorus cone in cells (per cent of dry weight) increases 1.5- or 2.5-fold in 3 days of their occurrence in the dark. P sub(org) is assimilated both in the dark and under different light conditions. Some spp (Platymonas viridis, Chaetoceros curvisetus) assimilate P sub(min) and P sub(org) simultaneously either in the dark or under faint light, whereas other spp (Phaeodactylum tricornutum, Goniaulax polyedra) assimilate only P sub(org). Lifetime excreta of cells and decomposition products of dead algae are P sub(org) sources. P sub(org) of the environment makes up 2 to 48 percent of P dissolved /total.},
